The HAL_SD_GetCardStatus function uses a 16-word array to store the SD card status. In contrast, SD_SendSDStatus initially reads 8 words when the FIFO is half-full. However, the function continues to read the remaining data until the DPSM is inactive, ensuring that all required data is retrieved. This approach is recommended in the reference manual, as shown below:



![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6818afbb-fd15-4fd9-ad7a-b42fc52175a6)


